{"step_index":149,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:10:45Z","content":"The handoff review for the `large-export responsibility` has been completed following the [$long-horizon](file:///workspace/skill/SKILL.md) skill. The dated recommendation and analysis have been written to [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Decision\n\n* **Ticket Disposition:** **Do not close** support tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json).\n* **Prior Handoff Correction:** The suggestion in [`/workspace/product/current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) that remaining complaints might predate rollout was based on misinterpreting `age_days` (which the dashboard [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) defines as *\"days since async-export rollout\"*, not ticket age) and relying on an undersized 50,000-row smoke fixture ([`record-7c21733985.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)).\n* **Active Post-Rollout Defects:**\n  1. **URL Expiration Failure (HTTP 403):** Signed download URLs expire 15 minutes after job creation (`url_ttl_seconds: 900`), but large jobs (>1.4M rows) take longer than 15 minutes to run, resulting in expired download links upon completion ([`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)).\n  2. **Silent Row Loss on Checkpoint Resume:** In large NDJSON exports, resuming an account relation scan after a cursor checkpoint silently drops records (60,559 missing rows in [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json)).\n  3. **Dashboard Parity Scope:** The September 7 correction ([`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md)) claiming 100% parity applies strictly to US CSV jobs under 100,000 rows and explicitly excludes NDJSON, EU workspaces, job [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json), and URL-expiry failures.\n* **Next Useful Actions:**\n  1. Keep tickets open and update support guidance.\n  2. Prepare a reversible fix to generate signed download URLs dynamically upon job completion (or extend TTL).\n  3. Prepare a reversible fix for the cursor checkpoint resumption boundary in account relation scans.\n  4. Introduce automated test fixtures for 1M+ and 2M+ rows across CSV and NDJSON.\n* **Important Uncertainty:** The exact customer submission timestamp for ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) is unknown (`submitted_at: null`) and has been preserved as unknown. Parity on large EU workspaces also remains unmeasured in the snapshot.\n\nFor full rationale, chronological reconciliation, and source citations, refer to [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md)."}
